<title>INDIA: Yield on 3-year Indian gilt set at 13.40 pct - RBI.</title>
<headline>Yield on 3-year Indian gilt set at 13.40 pct - RBI.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Monday it set a cut-off yield of 13.40 percent at the 20-billion rupee auction of three-year securities conducted earlier in the day.  </p>
<p>The RBI said it received 160 bids for 34.16 billion rupees, of which it accepted 93 for 20 billion. Partial allotment was made to 35 bidders, it added.</p>
<p>The weighted-average cut-off yield was 13.35 percent.</p>
</text>
